  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Parker executes the FY27 guide (7% organic midpoint) and consolidates Filtration Group, then grows mid-single-digit organically through the industrial and aerospace cycles. The Win Strategy and ~$220M of Filtration Group synergies lift EBITDA margin ~200bp to 30.5%, short of a full hit on the 30% adjusted-segment-margin target. Leverage from the $9.25B deal is serviced from ~$4.5-5B of annual owner FCF; CIRCOR Aerospace is treated as value-neutral.",
    "bull": "The broad-based recovery management guided to (every vertical positive in FY27 for the first time in years) runs for several years while commercial aerospace OEM rates and defense budgets lift the record $8.5B aerospace backlog into aftermarket annuity revenue. Data-centre liquid cooling and electromechanical actuation become real growth vectors, organic growth runs above the 4-6% framework, and margins beat the 30% target to ~32% EBITDA.",
    "bear": "Diversified Industrial (67% of sales) rolls over: agriculture/off-highway weakness spreads to construction and general industrial capex, tariffs and input inflation squeeze price-cost, and a commercial aerospace build-rate setback hits just as two large debt-funded integrations stretch management. Revenue falls ~6% in FY29, margins drop to ~26% before recovering to the FY26 level, synergies slip, and the exit multiple compresses to a cyclical 14x."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Parker is valued as a high-quality cyclical industrial on a strict owner-FCF basis: SBC expensed, share count flat, Filtration Group consolidated pro forma in both flows and net debt, and cyclicality carried in the bear scenario's flows rather than a discount-rate premium. The market price capitalises a premium industrial multiple that the 9% WACC owner-FCF build does not reach without bull-case margins.",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "Filtration Group revenue/EBITDA (~$1.9B / ~24%) are assumptions, not filed figures; the Q1 FY27 10-Q (Nov 2026) will give the first consolidated read",
      "Pro-forma net debt assumes the full $9.25B was debt-funded; any cash or CP mix changes the bridge dollar-for-dollar ($1B = ~$7.8/share)",
      "Industrial cycle timing: the bear case's FY29 downturn is a timing judgment",
      "CIRCOR Aerospace excluded; at ~23x EBITDA it is mildly value-dilutive to this model if it closes",
      "Terminal value is the majority of EV; WACC +/-1pp moves value ~15-20%"
    ]
  },
