    "net_debt_basis": "PRO FORMA for Filtration Group (closed 2026-08-13, after the balance-sheet date). FY26 10-K debt = non-current 6,766 + current 1,754 (CP ~1,048 + current maturities 706) = 8,520. The Metrics CSV TotalDebt of 9,226 double-counts the 706 current portion (LongTermDebt 7,472 already includes it) -- same XBRL trap as KEYS/NDSN. Plus 9,250 Filtration Group consideration, debt-funded ($7.75B new facilities + CP/notes) = 17,770 gross; less 501 cash = 17,269. Operating lease liabilities (213) excluded: US GAAP operating lease cost is already inside EBITDA (treatment B). Pension liability (224) and NCI (9) immaterial and not bridged.",
    "wacc_rationale": "USD build. Risk-free 4.3% (10y UST), ERP 5.0%, beta ~1.15 -> cost of equity ~10.0%; pre-tax cost of debt ~5.0% (4.0% after tax) at ~15% debt weight post-Filtration Group -> WACC ~9.1%, used as 9.0% in all three scenarios. Cyclicality is priced in the bear scenario's flows, not via a premium (risk charged once).",
    "lease_treatment": "Treatment (B): US GAAP operating-lease cost sits inside operating income/EBITDA; lease liabilities excluded from net debt.",
    "nci_treatment": "NCI of $9M is immaterial; flows not adjusted.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (operating company, cyclical US industrial) per dcf-methods routing; first valuation of PH, no prior DCF. FY0 build: GAAP operating income 5,068 + D&A 937 (depreciation 353 + intangible amortization 584) + SBC 179 = 6,184 pre-SBC EBITDA (28.8%); the margin path starts ~50bp lower (28.3% standalone FY0-equivalent) to absorb non-service pension/other expense (~104) and restructuring cash that sit between operating income and pretax income. Unlevered cash tax: 1,064 paid + 401 interest x 21% shield = ~1,148 on EBIT 5,068 = 22.6%, used as 22.5%. FILTRATION GROUP ($9.25B, closed 2026-08-13) is consolidated in BOTH flows and debt: assumed ~$1.9B annual revenue at ~24% EBITDA pre-synergy (~20x EBITDA paid), ~10.5 months in FY27 (+~8pp of FY27 growth) and the 1.5-month stub in FY28 (+~1pp). FY27 guidance of 5.5-8.5% reported/organic growth was issued 2026-08-06, before the close, and is read as excluding Filtration Group (reported and organic ranges are identical, which is impossible if a ~$1.9B acquisition were inside). The ~$220M year-3 synergy target is in the EBITDA ramp. CIRCOR Aerospace ($2.55B, ~$270M sales at >40% EBITDA, ~23x) is still pending regulatory approval and is EXCLUDED from both flows and debt -- treated as roughly value-neutral at the price paid; closing it would add ~$2.55B debt and ~$110M EBITDA. The working-capital charge (-12% of revenue change) also hits the acquired FY27/FY28 revenue step, which arrives with its own working capital: a conservative ~$200M (~$1.6/share) overcharge left in rather than special-cased. D&A path steps up for Filtration Group amortization then glides to 2.6% of revenue by Y10 so terminal D&A sits only modestly above capex (no perpetual amortization tax shield). Buybacks ($1,262M FY26, $1,766M FY25) fund the flat share count; Parker is a genuine repurchaser.",
